      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Nursing & Health Sciences - Missouri Valley University Skip to content REQUEST INFO REQUEST INFO VISIT VISIT APPLY APPLY GIVE GIVE Employment opportunity Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Instructor, Nursing & Health Sciences Missouri Valley University invites applications for Adjunct Instructor positions across multiple disciplines in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. Apply Now All Openings At a glance Location Schedule Department Reports to FLSA status Posted Deadline Closing date Compensation Estimated start Missouri Valley University invites applications for Adjunct Instructor positions across multiple disciplines in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. We seek dedicated educators committed to excellence in teaching, student success, and the university’s mission. Both on-campus and online teaching opportunities are available. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities Teach assigned course(s) as scheduled and outlined in the contract. Foster student success through engaging instruction and intellectual inquiry. Develop and distribute a comprehensive syllabus aligned with institutional guidelines. Implement initiatives to enhance student learning outcomes. Provide timely feedback and support to students. Maintain a respectful, inclusive, and productive learning environment. Collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues and administrators. Complete assigned administrative tasks with accuracy and adherence to deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, procedures, and requirements. Responsibilities listed are representative but not exhaustive of the position. Qualifications : Undergraduate program positions require a Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the relevant discipline from an accredited institution. Graduate program positions require a terminal degree in the discipline. A Terminal Degree (PhD, EdD, etc.) in the relevant discipline is preferred. Previous college or university teaching experience is preferred. Equivalent education, training, and experience may be considered. Physical Demands : Ability to teach and engage with students for extended periods. Capability to stand or sit for prolonged durations. Regular attendance is essential. Reasonable accommodations may be made for individuals with disabilities. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities : Strong ability to interact effectively with students, faculty, and diverse communities. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication, organizational, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently and effectively in an online or in-person setting. Commitment to professionalism and student-centered instruction. Familiarity with Google Workspace (preferred). Experience with Learning Management Systems (required). Online instructors must complete the MVU Online Masterclass. Work Environment : Online Instructors: Home office setting. On-Campus Instructors: Classroom and office settings. Required Technology (Online Instructors Only): Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Reliable high-speed Internet connection (Chrome browser required). Additional Information Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment is contingent upon a successful background check. Compensation varies by course, enrollment, and program type. Application Instructions Please send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to Human Resources at hr@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior approval from candidates. Ready to apply? Send your application materials to: hr@moval.edu The job description lists exactly what to include. Apply Now Questions about working at MVU? Email hr@moval.edu . Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. MVU adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs, and does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Working at MVU Personalized education for life skills and career success. That’s our mission, and every role at Missouri Valley University helps students reach it. Founded in 1889, MVU is a private university in Marshall, Missouri. Learn about MVU → Not quite the right fit? See every current opening at Missouri Valley University. Browse All Openings Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Students Working Professionals Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Athletics (opens in a new tab) LEARN Everywhere EXPLORE Missouri Valley University ACHIEVE Your Future DISCOVER Your Path Majors & Programs Tuition & Aid Pay My Bill MVU Online Student Engagement Admissions PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Students Working Professionals Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Athletics (opens in a new tab) LEARN Everywhere EXPLORE Missouri Valley University ACHIEVE Your Future DISCOVER Your Path Majors & Programs Tuition & Aid Pay My Bill MVU Online Student Engagement Admissions PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 Plan a Visit Directory Careers at MVU Give to MVU Explore About MVU Leadership Programs of Study Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Academic Schools Apply / Request Info Tuition & Financial Aid News 