    "https://www.moval.edu/employment/adjunct-instructor-of-communication-studies/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Communication Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Communication Studies - Missouri Valley University Skip to content REQUEST INFO REQUEST INFO VISIT VISIT APPLY APPLY GIVE GIVE Employment opportunity Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Instructor of Communication Studies The School of Arts and Humanities invites applications from qualified individuals for on-campus, face-to-face Adjunct Instructor of Communication Studies opportunities. Apply Now All Openings At a glance Location Main Campus (Marshall, MO) Schedule Department School of Arts and Humanities Reports to FLSA status Posted Deadline Closing date Compensation Estimated start The School of Arts and Humanities invites applications from qualified individuals for on-campus, face-to-face Adjunct Instructor of Communication Studies opportunities. Collegiality, professionalism, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence and the university mission are required. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Teach assigned course(s) such as Public Speaking, Interpersonal Communication, and Argumentation and Debate as specified in the course schedule and contract. Guide students to succeed through personal instruction and intellectual inquiry. Prepare and distribute to students a complete and comprehensive syllabus as per institutional guidelines for every course taught. Undertake and monitor initiatives to improve student learning. Respond to student work, communications, and requests in a timely manner. Maintain a positive, productive, and respectful classroom environment. Communicate, collaborate, and coordinate work with colleagues in a timely manner. Complete assigned or accepted responsibilities, including routine administrative tasks, with accuracy and attention to detail by established deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, requirements, and procedures. Representative, but not all inclusive, of the essential job functions/responsibilities required for this position. Qualifications Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Communication Studies from an accredited institution required. Terminal degree in Communication Studies or a related field from an accredited institution preferred. Previous teaching experience in a college or university setting is preferred. In evaluating candidates for this position, a combination of education, training, and experience which provides the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position may be considered. Physical Demands Stamina to teach classes as required. Ability to stand or sit for extended time periods. Regular attendance is a necessary and essential function. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to engage in effective interactions with students, employees, alumni, and other stakeholders, including individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Ability to think critically and solve problems independently. Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills. Ability to work effectively and independently with minimal supervision. Ability to provide an unwavering example of professionalism. Working knowledge of Google Workspace preferred. Working knowledge of Canvas or an equivalent learning management system required. Representative, but not all-inclusive, of the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for this position. Work Environment General classroom and office settings (on-campus Instructors) Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVU is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Compensation varies by course based on student enrollment and program type. Application Instructions Please send cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to Human Resources at hr@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Ready to apply? Send your application materials to: hr@moval.edu The job description lists exactly what to include. Apply Now Questions about working at MVU? Email hr@moval.edu . Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. MVU adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs, and does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Working at MVU Personalized education for life skills and career success. That’s our mission, and every role at Missouri Valley University helps students reach it. Founded in 1889, MVU is a private university in Marshall, Missouri. Learn about MVU → Not quite the right fit? See every current opening at Missouri Valley University. Browse All Openings Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Students Working Professionals Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Athletics (opens in a new tab) LEARN Everywhere EXPLORE Missouri Valley University ACHIEVE Your Future DISCOVER Your Path Majors & Programs Tuition & Aid Pay My Bill MVU Online Student Engagement Admissions PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Students Working Professionals Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Athletics (opens in a new tab) LEARN Everywhere EXPLORE Missouri Valley University ACHIEVE Your Future DISCOVER Your Path Majors & Programs Tuition & Aid Pay My Bill MVU Online Student Engagement Admissions PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 Plan a Visit Directory Careers at MVU Give to MVU Explore About MVU Leadership Programs of Study Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Academic Schools Apply / Request Info Tuition & Financial Aid News Events Calendar Athletics Resources Murrell Library Transcript Request Registrar’s Office Pay My Bill Student Check-In Career Development IT Help Desk Contact Us MyMoval Campus & Safety Report a Concern Daily Crime & Safety Alerts Counseling Center Viking Shuttle & Transportation Campus Map (PDF) Campus Store Copyright © 2026 Missouri Valley University Accreditation Student Consumer Information Title IX Annual Clery Report Disability Services Privacy Policy Powered by a Boat Full of Vikings Start typing and press enter to search Search... Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Students Working Professionals Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Athletics (opens in a new tab) LEARN Everywhere EXPLORE Missouri Valley University ACHIEVE Your Future DISCOVER Your Path Majors & Programs Tuition & Aid Pay My Bill MVU Online Student Engagement Admissions PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. Scroll to Top"
