    "https://www.moval.edu/employment/head-cheer-coach/": {
      "title": "Head Cheer Coach",
      "description": "Head Cheer Coach - Missouri Valley University Skip to content REQUEST INFO REQUEST INFO VISIT VISIT APPLY APPLY GIVE GIVE Employment opportunity Coaching & Athletics Head Cheer Coach Missouri Valley University seeks a talented, hard-working leader to serve as its next cheer coach. Apply Now All Openings At a glance Location Schedule Department Reports to FLSA status Posted Deadline Closing date Compensation Estimated start Missouri Valley University seeks a talented, hard-working leader to serve as its next cheer coach. The coach is responsible for leading and developing a competitive and game-day cheer program within the NAIA, UCA, and NCA. The coach promotes student-athlete success academically, athletically, and personally while representing the institution with professionalism and integrity. The coach will plan, organize, and direct all aspects of the cheer program, teaching and supervising stunts, choreography, sideline and competition routines, fostering a disciplined team culture and ensuring safety through proper training and risk management. Key Responsibilities Plan, organize, and direct all aspects of the cheer program. Meet or exceed institutional recruitment goals while Identifying, evaluating, and recruiting prospective student-athletes aligned with institutional and NAIA standards. Build relationships with high school and club cheer programs. Assist recruits through admissions and financial aid processes. Support retention and academic success of current team members Coordinate cheer participation at football, basketball, and other athletic events. Maintain compliance with NAIA and NCA rules, eligibility standards, and institutional policies. Manage team budget, travel, uniforms, and equipment. Schedule practices, competitions, and travel logistics. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree (required); Master’s preferred. Collegiate cheerleading and/or coaching experience. Knowledge of stunt safety, tumbling progression, and choreography. Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to recruit and retain student-athletes. CPR/AED and First Aid certification (or ability to obtain) Knowledge of NAIA rules and recruiting practices. Strong social media and program promotion skills. Evening and weekend travel required Ability to lift, spot, and demonstrate cheer techniques safely. Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, curriculum vitae, and references to hr@moval.edu (opens in a new tab) . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVU is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Ready to apply? Send your application materials to: hr@moval.edu The job description lists exactly what to include. Apply Now Questions about working at MVU? Email hr@moval.edu . Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. MVU adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs, and does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Working at MVU Personalized education for life skills and career success. That’s our mission, and every role at Missouri Valley University helps students reach it. Founded in 1889, MVU is a private university in Marshall, Missouri. Learn about MVU → Not quite the right fit? See every current opening at Missouri Valley University. Browse All Openings Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Students Working Professionals Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Athletics (opens in a new tab) LEARN Everywhere EXPLORE Missouri Valley University ACHIEVE Your Future DISCOVER Your Path Majors & Programs Tuition & Aid Pay My Bill MVU Online Student Engagement Admissions PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Students Working Professionals Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Athletics (opens in a new tab) LEARN Everywhere EXPLORE Missouri Valley University ACHIEVE Your Future DISCOVER Your Path Majors & Programs Tuition & Aid Pay My Bill MVU Online Student Engagement Admissions PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. PERSONALIZED EDUCATION FOR LIFE SKILLS AND CAREER SUCCESS. Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 Plan a Visit Directory Careers at MVU Give to MVU Explore About MVU Leadership Programs of Study Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Academic Schools Apply / Request Info Tuition & Financial Aid News Events Calendar Athletics Resources Murrell Library Transcript Request Registrar’s Office Pay My Bill Student Check-In Career Development IT Help Desk Contact Us MyMoval Campus & Safety Report a Concern Daily Crime & Safety Alerts Counseling Center Viking Shuttle & Transportation Campus Map (PDF) Campus Store Copyright © 2026 Missouri Valley University Accreditation Student Consumer Information Title IX Annual Clery Report Disability Services Privacy Policy Powered by a Boat Full of Vikings Start typing and press enter to search Search... Request Info Visit Apply Give Prospective Students Current Students Graduate Stud